- **FAN-C1** is the finding I'd most want acted on and it appears in neither the packet nor the prior-pass notes: the Painted Porch curation rule isn't a standalone object. It's the same rule as his Reading List Email, running since May 2009 — *"I would rather recommend nothing than recommend a book that ends up letting people down,"* explicitly at the cost of affiliate revenue. That converts a static object into a seventeen-year through-line and gives the Rabbit Hole's own falsification test a second instance instead of resting on Annapolis alone.
